  "body": "### What is the issue with the HTML Standard?\n\n[Step 2](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/#abort-a-navigateevent:~:text=Signal%20abort%20on%20event%27s%20abort%20controller%20given%20reason%2E) of #abort-a-navigateevent signals an abort on the event's abort controller. This is called as part of the [failure steps](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/#navigate-event-firing:abort-a-navigateevent) called from #inner-navigate-event-firing. However, when implementing this, the following tests fail, because the abort signal is not listed.\n- https://github.com/web-platform-tests/wpt/blob/c05ece9d6f47c4e8ca20c3625a12206fe4208519/navigation-api/ordering-and-transition/navigate-same-document-intercept-reject.html#L46-L47\n- https://github.com/web-platform-tests/wpt/blob/c05ece9d6f47c4e8ca20c3625a12206fe4208519/navigation-api/ordering-and-transition/reload-intercept-reject.html#L46-L47\n\nGecko's old (pre-precommithandler) implementation passed these tests, so I assume that there were refactorings and the tests need to be updated.\n\ncc @noamr ",
